      </problem>
    </exercise>
    <heading level="1">Writing Exercises</heading>
    <exercise number="387" has_solution="true">
      <problem>
        <list type="ordered">
          <item>ⓐ Simplify $$\sqrt{\frac{27}{3}}$$ and explain all your steps.</item>
          <item>ⓑ Simplify $$\sqrt{\frac{27}{5}}$$ and explain all your steps.</item>
          <item>ⓒ Why are the two methods of simplifying square roots different?</item>
        </list>
      </problem>
      <solution>
        <paragraph>Answers will vary.</paragraph>
      </solution>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="388" has_solution="true">
      <problem>
        <list type="ordered">
          <item>ⓐ Approximate $$\frac{1}{\sqrt{2}}$$ by dividing $$\frac{1}{1.414}$$ using long division without a calculator.</item>
          <item>ⓑ Rationalizing the denominator of $$\frac{1}{\sqrt{2}}$$ gives $$\frac{\sqrt{2}}{2}.$$ Approximate $$\frac{\sqrt{2}}{2}$$ by dividing $$\frac{1.414}{2}$$ using long division without a calculator.</item>
          <item>ⓒ Do you agree that rationalizing the denominator makes calculations easier? Why or why not?</item>
        </list>
      </problem>
      <solution>
        <paragraph>$$9 5 9 5$$</paragraph>
      </solution>
    </exercise>
